From c4e227a3559c9508b922d47071febc8559d7eb11 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: colum <git@volf.co>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 11:12:36 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] 0297 dsv41: TF_DS_KEYS_PROFILE (off by default): the
 pruned selection's width and key-encoding class on the profile line

The localization of the TF_DS_IDX_FUSED selection divergence (runs/fused-followup-20261121): round.zig's
candidate-source selection records the keys' width and whether the kit's _score_keys or the fused key fold (0206)
wrote them; key_prof.zig aggregates per class and prints a key_profile line beside prefill_profile_ms. idx_fused.zig
gains the host-side check: the fold's flipped keys reverse the pruned picks across the sign bit at every width in
16,384 < width <= 65,536 (the fold's engagement window in the follow-up tree) and agree inside one sign class.
